[38;5;252m[1m## Two things worth knowing[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The abort/misuse checks run in forked children, and [38;5;10mfork()[0m in a multithreaded process can inherit a held malloc or loader lock and wedge the child. [38;5;10mtools/run_tests.sh[0m and [38;5;10mtools/feature_matrix.sh[0m therefore pass [38;5;10m--test-threads=1[0m, and children arm [38;5;10malarm()[0m so a wedge surfaces as a loud failure instead of a hang.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The [38;5;10mcovered by test[0m column is produced by matching each row's C function against the symbols each test resolves. It proves the entry point is driven differentially by a passing test, and the tests sweep trigger dimensions exhaustively where they are small (every [38;5;10moutlen[0m 0..=66, every truncated ciphertext length, every single-bit tag flip, every [38;5;10minlen & 7[0m case, all four base64 variants, all 256 secretstream tag values, out-of-range enums). It does not by itself prove every exact trigger string was constructed — that caveat is stated in both tables rather than glossed over. Two [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m rows describe conditions the C accepts rather than rejects ([38;5;10mARGON2_MAX_TIME[0m/[38;5;10mMAX_MEMORY[0m are both [38;5;10m0xFFFFFFFF[0m, so [38;5;10mu32::MAX[0m passes validation and the C then attempts 4 billion passes / 4 TiB); those are called out in place, with the reachable over-maximum rejection tested through the public wrappers instead.[0m[0m
